{
  "case_id": "2022-21-454",
  "document_hash": "3c5942d83fce1e0461d572acc3e92a331235447fc23e31dc1dbebb3325f09cf3",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c5942d83fce1e0461d572acc3e92a331235447fc23e31dc1dbebb3325f09cf3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c5942d83fce-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:03 a.m.\nAPPEARANCES:\nDAMIEN M. SCHIFF, ESQUIRE, Sacramento, California; on behalf of the Petitioners.\nBRIAN H. FLETCHER, Principal Deputy Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c5942d83fce1e0461d572acc3e92a331235447fc23e31dc1dbebb3325f09cf3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c5942d83fce-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Schiff, can -- can intrastate, purely intrastate, navigable bodies of water be waters of the United States?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c5942d83fce1e0461d572acc3e92a331235447fc23e31dc1dbebb3325f09cf3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c5942d83fce-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But doesn't that, Mr. Schiff, ignore the import of 1344(g)(1), which really specifically says that when we're talking about waters, we're talking about -- including their wetlands, 1344(g)(1) says."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c5942d83fce1e0461d572acc3e92a331235447fc23e31dc1dbebb3325f09cf3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c5942d83fce-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: But -- but counsel, why -- why is it that your conception of this does not relate in any way to Congress's primary objective? Do you dispute that the primary objective as stated in the statute, I guess it's at 1251, is that Congress cared about making sure that the chemical, physical, and biological integrity of the nation's waters was protected?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c5942d83fce1e0461d572acc3e92a331235447fc23e31dc1dbebb3325f09cf3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c5942d83fce-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: A footnote, why didn't they use the word they used elsewhere, \"abutting\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c5942d83fce1e0461d572acc3e92a331235447fc23e31dc1dbebb3325f09cf3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c5942d83fce-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What is the government's theory of how the water from the Sacketts' property gets to the wetlands?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c5942d83fce1e0461d572acc3e92a331235447fc23e31dc1dbebb3325f09cf3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c5942d83fce-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Now, as I understand it, there's a difference between groundwater and subsurface flows. Am I correct about that too?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c5942d83fce1e0461d572acc3e92a331235447fc23e31dc1dbebb3325f09cf3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c5942d83fce-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Schiff, do you think there's any third position? I mean, I -- I understand that you don't like the significant nexus test, but I'm going back really to Justice Kavanaugh's point about, you know, take something like you just create a dam so that -- and the dam breaks up any idea that there is a continuous surface connection."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c5942d83fce1e0461d572acc3e92a331235447fc23e31dc1dbebb3325f09cf3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c5942d83fce-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If we're going to have something more than a continuous water surface test like we did in Riverside Bayview, if we're going to, excuse me, expand beyond that, why not just look at the geographic proximity between this property and -- and the lake?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c5942d83fce1e0461d572acc3e92a331235447fc23e31dc1dbebb3325f09cf3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c5942d83fce-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And -- and -- and that is what's being asked, is --is a person who purchased a property with -- with a sewer hookup a block from the lake with a subdivision between you and the lake and a road on the other side is supposed to know that that's a water of the United States, that piece of property, or else what?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2022-21-454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c5942d83fce1e0461d572acc3e92a331235447fc23e31dc1dbebb3325f09cf3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c5942d83fce-0002-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "they were threatened with significant civil and administrative penalties and, of course, also the continuing liability of having to restore the property to the way it was before they began any work."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c5942d83fce1e0461d572acc3e92a331235447fc23e31dc1dbebb3325f09cf3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c5942d83fce-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "wetlands are covered as waters of the United States, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-21-454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c5942d83fce1e0461d572acc3e92a331235447fc23e31dc1dbebb3325f09cf3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c5942d83fce-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: -- is -- under the position of the federal government, is a ecological and biological connection between wetlands and navigable waters enough to bring the wetlands into coverage? In other words, dry land between it, but underneath -- you know, we had that case in Hawaii that indicated how far"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c5942d83fce1e0461d572acc3e92a331235447fc23e31dc1dbebb3325f09cf3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c5942d83fce-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Can I ask you to clarify some of the answers that you just gave to the Chief Justice? I mean, the statutory language is of adjacency, and at certain points in your answer, you suggested that the significant effects test is really just the test that you use to evaluate whether there's sufficient adjacency."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-21-454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c5942d83fce1e0461d572acc3e92a331235447fc23e31dc1dbebb3325f09cf3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c5942d83fce-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: And they need not be adjacent. So what Justice Kagan's question is getting to -- and I want to make certain I understand it because it's important to me -- the significant nexus test is separate and apart, so it can be not adjacent, but so long as there's a significant nexus, it's still covered, it's untethered from 1344(g) in that respect?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-454",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3c5942d83fce1e0461d572acc3e92a331235447fc23e31dc1dbebb3325f09cf3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c5942d83fce-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: So how about 3,000\nfeet? Could be?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c5942d83fce1e0461d572acc3e92a331235447fc23e31dc1dbebb3325f09cf3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c5942d83fce-0005-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 109,
        "start": 109
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Could -- would you win if 1344(g) had not been enacted?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Damien M. Schiff",
      "case_id": "2022-21-454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c5942d83fce1e0461d572acc3e92a331235447fc23e31dc1dbebb3325f09cf3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c5942d83fce-0005-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 122,
        "start": 121
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SCHIFF: Whatever the deficiencies in the line-drawing problem test, they pale in comparison to the significant nexus test. In response to Justice Thomas --Thomas's question about the channels of commerce, the significant nexus test is far, far broader than a traditional understanding of the channels of commerce, as shown by this very case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c5942d83fce1e0461d572acc3e92a331235447fc23e31dc1dbebb3325f09cf3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c5942d83fce-0005-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 126,
        "start": 125
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 11:52 a.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
    {
